{
  "name": "Real Estate to Instagram",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nA licensed Toronto MLS feed comes in on the left. Six properties. Each one is\nasked two separate questions - **is it notable enough to post**, and **are we\nallowed to post it** - and those are not the same question.\n\nOut the other end: **two full posts, two market notes, two skipped.**\n\nEvery skip is written down with its reason. A content system that silently\ndrops things is a content system nobody trusts by month three.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2040,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Qualifying and publishing are different questions\n\nToronto sold prices are not public record. They live in the MLS, and the feed\nthat carries them - **VOW**, the sold-data tier - says the data may only be\nshown behind a login, to a registered consumer, and **may not be monetised**. A\npublic Instagram post of someone else's sale is the exact thing that rule exists\nto stop.\n\n**And the photos are a second, separate problem.** Listing photos belong to the\nlisting brokerage or the photographer they hired - not to the board, and not to\nwhoever holds the data feed. Putting another brokerage's photo into your branded\ntemplate is a copyright claim, and they will see the post.\n\nSo there are **three** answers, not two:\n\n- **We listed it** - our photos, our seller, our sale. Post it in full.\n- **We were in the deal, or it is genuine market news** - post a **market\n  note**: neighbourhood, price band, our own artwork. No borrowed photo, no\n  street address.\n- **Neither** - do not post, and log why.\n\nThe middle lane is the whole design, and it is the answer to the client's\nscreening question.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "b3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1570,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Two things worth saying out loud\n\n**Everything that writes or publishes is greyed out on purpose** - the approval\nping, both Instagram calls, and all three database writes. You can run the whole\nthing against a real feed, read every verdict, and leave nothing behind.\n\n**Dedupe is keyed on the address, not the MLS number.** This is the gotcha that\nbites everyone: when a property is taken off the market and re-listed it gets a\n**brand new MLS number**. Dedupe on that and the same house goes out three times\nover one spring, which is precisely the failure the client asked to avoid.\n\n**The feed node is the swap point.** Which source belongs there depends entirely\non what the client is licensed for - see `data-sources.md`. Everything to the\nright of it is unchanged either way.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "b3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1010,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
